{"name":"Lava Lamp","hex":"#eb7135","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lava lamp","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of lamp, typically used more for decoration than illumination, in which the gentle flow of randomly-shaped clumps of wax purportedly suggests the flowing of lava."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lava_lamp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lava lamp","blocks":[{"text":"A lava lamp is a decorative lamp that was invented in 1963 by British entrepreneur Edward Craven Walker, the founder of the lighting company Mathmos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Lava_lamps_%2816136876840%29.jpg/330px-Lava_lamps_%2816136876840%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_lamp","wikidata":"Q839679"},{"title":"Lava","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is magma that has been expelled from the interior of a terrestrial planet or a moon onto its surface. Lava may be erupted at a volcano or through a fracture in the crust, on land or underwater, usually at temperatures from 800 to 1,200 °C. Lava may be erupted directly onto the land surface or onto the sea floor or it may be ejected into the atmosphere before falling back down. The solid volcanic rock resulting from subsequent cooling of the molten material is often also called lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava","wikidata":"Q40157"},{"title":"Lava (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is a color that is a purplish shade of red. It is named after the color of volcanic lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Pahoeoe_fountain_